T04-W1 review follow-up (2026-11-09)

Finding preserved: `workflow/tasks/student-tickets/review-T04.md` identified that `browser-inspection-server.js` used `candidate.startsWith(root)`, allowing a sibling path with the same string prefix to be considered contained.

Fix: replaced the string-prefix check with `isWithinRoot(rootPath, candidatePath)`, which uses `path.relative` and rejects a result equal to `..`, a result starting with `..${path.sep}`, or an absolute relative result. The server now starts only when run as the main module and exports the helper so the browser harness can exercise the exact check.

Direct check command, from `src/codeclinic`:
`node -e "const a=require('node:assert/strict');const p=require('node:path');const {isWithinRoot,root}=require('./test/browser-inspection-server');a.equal(isWithinRoot(root,p.join(root,'index.html')),true);a.equal(isWithinRoot(root,p.resolve(root+'-private','secret')),false);a.equal(isWithinRoot(root,p.resolve(root,'..','secret')),false);console.log('PASS: in-root accepted; sibling-prefix and parent escapes rejected')"`
Result: `PASS: in-root accepted; sibling-prefix and parent escapes rejected`.

Browser rerun command: `node .\test\browser-inspection.js`, using the locally served optimized build and synthetic session/CSRF/ticket responses. Result: PASS; path-containment assertions passed, viewport/document/body width were 320, no horizontal overflow, Tab reached the title and submit, and Space-submit focused the first invalid field with its associated error. Full JSON and output: `implementation-T04-browser.json` and `implementation-T04-W1-browser-run.log`; screenshots: `browser-inspection-320-top.png` and `browser-inspection-320-bottom.png`. Both the local server and Chrome processes were stopped after the run.

No production source, dependencies, checklist, current-state file, review report, or approval state was changed.
